 "text": "Hey, how are you doing? Roughly one hand bag per rim, more than that and you' carrying more than you ride. A basket is great for fruits and veggies that you eat right off the bike. A bag that clips onto the rack is good for regular shelves. Then a front pannier system is worth looking at. Then a small shop is perfect. You can leave it on your bike and pick up any small items you need. It' heavy for long rides and blocks your arms. Stick to the bag if you can.",
